    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0636" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.248/466</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 10613</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-30">March 30, 1943</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        7.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my strictly confidential
                    despatch No. 10604 of March 29, 1943,<anchor n="22" xml:id="d565-f1"/> reporting
                    that on Admiral Beauregard’s behalf I <pb facs="0637" n="625" xml:id="pg625"/>
                    had taken up certain matters with President Vargas, I have the honor to report
                    that yesterday Admiral Beauregard brought to my attention another letter from
                    Admiral Ingram,<anchor n="23" xml:id="d565-f2"/> in which he requested Admiral
                    Beauregard to endeavor to obtain from the Air Minister action in eight different
                    cases. With this in mind, Admiral Beauregard addressed a pertinent communication
                    to Dr. J. P. Salgado Filho in which the eight different cases were set out in
                    lettered paragraphs “<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>” to “<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >h</hi>”, a copy of which I transmit herewith.</p>
                <p>In accordance with Admiral Beauregard’s desire, I shall bring this memorandum
                    also to the attention of President Vargas this afternoon.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d565-a1.xml" xpointer="d565-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d565-f1" n="22" xml:id="d565-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; Adm. A. T. Beauregard, Chief of the American Naval Mission in
                    Brazil, complained that the Brazilian Air Ministry was not making the best use
                    of planes at its disposal (832.248/462).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d565-f2" n="23" xml:id="d565-f2-content">
                <p>Vice Adm. Jonas H. Ingram, Commander of the South Atlantic Force.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
